// Cross-repo consume fails closed on the WHOLE commit (SPEC.md SS6 / the
// SS7 doc comment: "whole-record consumption claims fail closed on the
// whole commit when they cross a repository boundary (a structural
// violation)"). SPEC-DRIVEN: written and checked via `forge goal` before
// any implementation existed.
//
// One half of a deliberate pair with fact_retraction_fails_open.th: SS7
// states two DIFFERENT failure postures for two different severities of
// problem, and that distinction is exactly the kind of thing easy to
// silently conflate by hand (treat both as fail-open, or both as
// fail-closed). This contract pins the fail-CLOSED half: a commit whose
// `consumes` claim illegally crosses a repository boundary is invalid
// OUTRIGHT, unconditionally -- regardless of whether the rest of the
// commit would otherwise have been fine.
//
// `otherwise_valid` stands in for whatever every other check on this
// commit concludes. The `ens` requires the result to be false whenever
// `is_cross_repo_consume` is true, no matter what `otherwise_valid` is --
// an implementation that lets a cross-repo consume slip through because
// the rest of the commit looked fine cannot satisfy it.

fn commit_valid(is_cross_repo_consume: bool, otherwise_valid: bool) -> bool
  req true
  ens result == (!is_cross_repo_consume && otherwise_valid)
  fx  pure
{
  !(is_cross_repo_consume) && otherwise_valid
}
